$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the One-Pot Synthesis of
Substituted 2-Aminothiophenes 3 A mixture of carbonyl compound (3.0
mmol), nitrile (3.3 mmol), sulfur (4.5 mmol), L-proline (0.3 mmol), and
DMF (3.0 mL) in a 50 mL round bottom flask was stirred at 60°C for 10-24
h. The crude product was directly purified through flash chromatography.
The desired product 3.
2-Amino-4,5,6,7-tetrahydrobenzo[b]thiophene-3-carbonitrile (Table 2,
entry 2) [1] 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 4.56 (bs, 2H), 2.52-2.46 (m,
4H), 1.85-1.73 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 160.1, 132.3,
120.6, 115.5, 88.6, 24.5, 24.1, 23.4, 22.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Gewald reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An efficient one-pot synthesis of substituted 2-aminothiophenes via
three-component Gewald reaction catalyzed by L-proline
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
