$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Gewald Reaction
Carbonyl compound (2 mmol), malononitrile, or ethyl cyanoacetate (2 mmol)
and sulfur (2 mmol) were added in ionic liquid BmimBF4 or BmimPF6 (2 mL).
The reaction mixture was stirred for 3-8 h at 50°C. Reaction was
monitored by thin-layer chromatography (TLC). After the reaction, the
resulting mixture was extracted with Et2O (3 x 10 ml). The combined
ethereal solution was evaporated to give the crude product, which was
purified by recrystallization or preparative TLC (silica gel). After
isolation of the product, the remainder of the ionic liquids containing
catalyst EDDA was dried for 2 h under vacuum at 50°C. The next run was
performed under identical reaction conditions. Table 1, Entry 6, 4e,
yield 89%. Mpa/°C: 146-147; Lit.mp/°C: 147-148[2a].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, green chemistry-solvent, Gewald reaction, ionic liquid
used, reaction in BmimPF6 gave similar yield
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Organic reactions in ionic liquids. Gewald synthesis of 2-aminothiophenes
catalyzed by ethylenediammonium diacetate
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Hu, Yi; Chen, Zhen-Chu; Le, Zhang-Gao; Zheng, Qin-Guo
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2004), 34(20), 3801-3806

