$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4.1. General experimental procedure: A 50ml round-bottomed flask was
charged with α-methylene carbonyl compound 10 (5 mmol), malononitrile 11
(5 mmol), and 25 ml H2O, which was stirred for 20 min under heating or
ultrasound irradiation. Subsequently, sodium polysulfide 12 (5 mmol) was
added and stirred at 70°C under conventional heating or ultrasound
irradiation. The mixture became turbid at the end of the reaction, which
was poured into cold water. The crude product was isolated by filtration
and was further purified by recrystallization with ethanol to afford pure
2-aminothiophenes. All the products were isolated, and their isolated
yields are given in Table 2. Identities of the products were established
by comparison of their physical and spectral data with those of reported
compounds. Product 13a, yield 84%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, ultrasound ((40KHz), Gewald reaction, mechanism
studied, 300W), optimization study, optimized on solvent and reagent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM First Gewald reaction ignited by sodium polysulfide: greener
ultrasound-promoted synthesis of substituted 2-aminothiophenes in the
absence of catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Liang, Chengyuan; Lei, Dong; Wang, Xiuzhen; Zhang, Qingqing; Yao, Qizheng
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Sulfur Chemistry (2013), 34(5), 458-463

