$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.1. Typical procedure. A mixture of 1a (311
μL, 3 mmol), 2a (198 mg, 3 mmol), and sulfur (96 mg, 3 mmol) in H2O (0.9
mL) and Et3N (418 μL, 3.0 mmol) was stirred at room temperature for 6 h
until TLC showed complete disappearance of the starting materials. The
product, which precipitated at the end of the reaction, was separated by
fitration. The pure product was obtained by recrystallization of the
precipitates using EtOAc/hexane mixture. Ethyl
2-amino-5,7-dihydro-4H-thieno[2,3-c]pyran-3-carboxylate (3fb). Yield:
98%, Yellow solid. Reactant: 1f+2b, time: 5 h. mp: 117-118°C; 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.33-1.36 (t, J = 7.12, 14.23 Hz, 3H), 2.82-2.84 (m, 2H),
3.91-3.93 (t, J = 5.59, 11.19 Hz, 2H), 4.25-4.30 (q, J = 7.11, 14.22,
21.34 Hz, 2H), 4.56-4.57 (t, J = 3.32, 10.69 Hz, 2H), 6.11 (s, 2H) ppm;
13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3) δ 14.8, 28.1, 59.9, 65.0, 65.3, 105.7, 115.0,
130.7, 162.8, 166.3 ppm. (KBr, cm-1) 3433, 3325, 2945, 2902, 2846, 1654,
1587, 1265, 1083, 1018 cm-1; MS (70 eV): m/z 229 (M+2), 228 (M+1), 227
(M+), 198, 124, 125, 29; Anal. Calcd for C10H13NO3S: C, 52.85; H, 5.77.
Found: C, 52.63; H, 5.80.
