$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Synthesis of thiophene 2-amino-3-carbethoxy esters (2a-e) under Microwave
Irradiation: General Procedure A An appropriate ketone (0.05 mol), sulfur
(1.6 g; 0.05 mol), ethyl cyanoacetate (5.8 g; 0.05 mol), and diethylamine
(3.65 g; 0.05 mol) were mixed together in methanol (4 ml) in a 100-ml
open tall glass beaker. The beaker was irradiated with MW at 350 W for
2-5 min (Table 1). On chilling, the reaction mixture produced the desired
product, which was filtered, washed with chilled aq. ethanol, and dried.
2-Amino-3-carbethoxy-4,5,6,7-tetrahydrobenzo(b)thiophene (2a): Yield
10.48 g, 90%. mp 113- 115°C; IR (KBr) cm-1: 3414 (NH); 1649 (CO); 1H NMR
(CDCl3) δ ppm: 1.34, 3H, t, CH3 at 3; 1.62, 2H, s, CH2 at 5 & 6; 2.61,
4H, s, CH2 at 4 & 7; 4.2, 2H, s, NH2, 4.32, 2H, q, CH2 at 3.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient synthesis of substituted 2-amino-3-carbethoxythiophenes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kathiravan, M. K.; Shishoo, C. J.; Chitre, T. S.; Mahadik, K. R.; Jain,
K. S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2007), 37(23), 4273-4279

