$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Compounds 2 (20 mmol) and 3 (20 mmol) were
dissolved in absolute ethanol (30 mL). Then, sulfur (22 mmol) and
catalyst 1 (3.70 g) were added and the mixture was refluxed at 80 °C for
4 h. The reaction mixture was cooled to room temperature and the solid
catalyst was filtered off. The solution poured into an ice-water mixture
(60 mL) and the precipitation was filtered off, washed with cold water,
and dried in vacuo. Ethyl
2-amino-4,5,6,7-tetrahydrobenzo[b]thiophene-3-carboxylate (5h). Starting
compounds: Compound 2h, Compound 3b; Yield 86%. Mp 115 (115)°C. IR (KBr,
cm-1) 3420, 3310, 2900, 1660, 1590; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz) δ 5.94 (s,
2H), 4.25 (q, 2H), 2.69-2.60 (m, 2H), 2.49-2.43 (m, 2H), 1.76-1.66 (m,
4H), 1.33 (t, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 166.1, 161.7, 132.5, 117.6,
105.8, 59.4, 26.9, 24.5, 23.3, 22.8, 14.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM solid-supported catalyst, piperazine supported on amorphous silica used
as catalyst, Gewald reaction, catalyst prepared and used
