$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the One-Pot Synthesis of Substituted
2-Aminothiophenes 3 A mixture of carbonyl compound (3.0 mmol), nitrile
(3.3 mmol), sulfur (4.5 mmol), L-proline (0.3 mmol), and DMF (3.0 mL) in
a 50 mL round bottom flask was stirred at 60°C for 10-24 h. The crude
product was directly purified through flash chromatography. The desired
product 3. Ethyl
2-amino-4,5,6,7,-tetrahydrobenzo[b]thiophene-3-carboxylate (Table 2,
entry 1) [1] 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 5.94 (bs, 2H), 4.28 (q, J = 4.0
and 12.0 Hz, 2H), 2.74-2.71 (m, 2H), 2.52-2.51 (m, 2H), 1.81-1.75 (m,
4H), 1.35 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 166.1,
161.7, 132.5, 117.6, 105.8, 59.4, 26.9, 24.5, 23.3, 22.8, 14.5.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimized on amount of catalyst, solvent, temperature and time for yield,
Gewald reaction, optimization study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An efficient one-pot synthesis of substituted 2-aminothiophenes via
three-component Gewald reaction catalyzed by L-proline
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
