$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.1. Typical procedure. A mixture of 1a (311
μL, 3 mmol), 2a (198 mg, 3 mmol), and sulfur (96 mg, 3 mmol) in H2O (0.9
mL) and Et3N (418 μL, 3.0 mmol) was stirred at room temperature for 6 h
until TLC showed complete disappearance of the starting materials. The
product, which precipitated at the end of the reaction, was separated by
fitration. The pure product was obtained by recrystallization of the
precipitates using EtOAc/hexane mixture. Product 3bb. Yield: 95%, time: 7
h. Reactant: 1b+2b.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, Gewald reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient three-component Gewald reactions under Et3N/H2O conditions
