$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the One-Pot Synthesis of
Substituted 2-Aminothiophenes 3 A mixture of carbonyl compound (3.0
mmol), nitrile (3.3 mmol), sulfur (4.5 mmol), L-proline (0.3 mmol), and
DMF (3.0 mL) in a 50 mL round bottom flask was stirred at 60°C for 10-24
h. The crude product was directly purified through flash chromatography.
The desired product 3.
2-Amino-5,6,7,8-tetrahydro-4H-cyclohepta[b]thiophene-3-carbonitrile
(Table 2, entry 13) [9] 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 4.28 (bs, 2H), 2.62
(t, J = 4.0 Hz, 2H) 2.58 (t, J = 4.0 Hz, 2H), 1.82-1.79 (m, 2H),
1.66-1.64 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 157.9, 136.8, 123.8,
91.9, 31.8, 29.4, 29.1, 28.0, 27.2.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Gewald reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An efficient one-pot synthesis of substituted 2-aminothiophenes via
three-component Gewald reaction catalyzed by L-proline
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Tao; Huang, Xian-Gui; Liu, Jia; Li, Bo; Wu, Jin-Jin; Chen,
Kai-Xian; Zhu, Wei-Liang; Xu, Xiao-Yong; Zeng, Bu-Bing
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synlett (2010), (9), 1351-1354

