$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Ketone (1.0mmol), nitrile (1.0 mmol),
elemental sulfur (0.035 g, 1.1 mmol), Mg/ La mixed oxide (1mole %) and
2ml of dry ethanol were mixed and placed in a 10ml pressure tube. The
mixture was subjected to microwave irradiation (MicroSynth, 160W, 150
psi, 78 °C, 85Hz) for the time indicated in Table 1 and then diluted with
chloroform (5 ml) and filtered. The solid was rinsed with chloroform (2 ×
3ml) and the combined extracts were concentrated and purified by normal
chromatography to afford the corresponding 2-aminothiophenes. The
spectral data (IR and NMR) of all products matched in all respects with
reported data. In the case of conventional heating, the reactants, as
above in 20ml ethanol, were heated at reflux (78 °C) for the time
indicated in Table 1. When the reaction was complete (thin-layer
chromatography; methanol/chloroform 1/9), solvent was removed by
evaporation under reduced pressure and the reaction mixture was diluted
with 10ml of chloroform and filtered. After evaporation of the solvent,
themixture was purified by normal column chromatography to give the
desired products. Spectral data of synthesized products are given in
Table 3. Entry 1: Conventional yield: 91%. Entry 8: Microwave yield: 88%.
2-Amino-4-phenylthiophene-3-carbonitrile. Mp: Found: 142°C; Reported:
142°C [6]; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ 6.96 (s, 2H), 7.14 (s, 1H), 7.43- 7.54 (m,
5H); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ 79.8, 115.4, 127.7, 129.4, 129.9, 136.4, 139.1,
154.2; IR (KBr) 2195, 3330, 3441 cm-1. Anal. calcd. for C11H8N2S: C,
65.97; H, 4.03; N, 13.99; S, 16.01. Found: C, 65.93; H, 4.01; N, 13.95;
S, 15.98.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation (160W), Gewald reaction, 85Hz, pressured tube used,
conventional heating gave the same yield in 70m
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Mg/La mixed oxide as an efficient heterogeneous basic catalyst for
synthesis of 2-aminothiophenes under microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Moeinpour, Farid; Dorostkar, Nadieh; Vafaei, Majid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthetic Communications (2012), 42(16), 2367-2374

