$DATUM Ethyl 2-amino-5-benzoyl-4-methylthiophene-3-carboxylate (1) A mixture of
benzoylacetone (10 mmol), ethyl cyanoacetate (10 mmol), sulfur (10 mmol),
and diethylamine (10 mmol) was heated at 70 °C with stirring in 20 cm3
absolute ethanol for 4 h. The reaction mixture was left overnight in a
refrigerator at 0 °C. The solid product was collected by filtration,
washed with ethanol, dried, and recrystallized from ethanol to afford 1.
Yield 85%. M.p.: 215-217 °C; IR (KBr): ν = 3,652 (NH2), 1,690, 1,620 (2
CO) cm-1; 1H NMR (500 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 1.32 (t, J= 6.9 Hz, 3H, CH3),
2.22 (s, 3H, CH3), 4.30 (q, 2H, J= 7.2 Hz, CH2), 6.55 (br.s, 2H, NH2),
7.44-7.94 (m, 5H, Ar-H) ppm; 13C NMR (125.7 MHz, DMSO-d6): δ = 23.1,
24.3, 39.8, 40.1, 40.2, 115.3, 116.8, 119.5, 125.6, 129.1, 143.7, 161.2,
167.9 ppm; MS: m/z (%) = 289 (33) [M+]. Molecular Formula: C15H15NO3S
