$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2-Amino-3-cyano-4-phenylthiophene (4a),
2-Amino-3-cyano-4-(4-methyl-phenyl)thiophene (4b) and
2-Amino-3-cyano-4-(4-methoxy-phenyl)thiophene (4c) General Procedure
Equimolar amount of α -cyano-β -phenyl crotononitrile (3a) (1.68 g, 0.01
mol), or α -cyano-β -(4-methylphenyl) crotononitrile (3b) (1.82 g, 0.01
mol) or α -cyano-β -(4-methoxyphenyl) crotnonitrile (3c) (1.98 g, 0.01
mol) and sulfur (0.32 g, 0.01 mol) in absolute ethanol (20 mL) containing
triethylamine (0.5 mL) were heated under reflux for 3 h. The solid
product, in each case, thus formed upon dilution with water containing
few drops of hydrochloric acid, which was collected by filtration.
2-Amino-3-cyano-4-(4-methyl-phenyl)thiophene (4b). Canary-yellow crystals
(from ethanol), yield 85% (1.81 g). m.p. 95°C. IR ν (cm-1) = 3577-3476
(NH2), 3055 (CH aromatic), 2987 (CH3), 2210 (CN), 1638 (C=C). 1H NMR δ =
2.21 (s, 3H, CH3), 4.37 (s, 2H, NH2, D2O exchangeable), 6.30 (s, 2H,
thiophene H-5), 7.25-7.30 (m, 4H, C6H5). Anal. Calcd for C12H10N2S (M/e =
214): C, 67.26; H, 4.70; N, 13.07; S, 14.96; found: C, 67.09; H, 4.90; N,
12.89; S, 15.35%.
