$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-Allyl-2-amino-5-phenylthiophene-3-carboxamide (C2,6): General Procedure
B (three-component reactions of aldehyde or ketones, cyanoacetamide and
sulfur). In a 20 ml vial added into N-allyl-2-cyanoacetamide (1.24 g, 10
mmol), 2-phenylacetaldehyde (1.20 g, 10 mmol) and sulfur (320 mg, 10
mmol) and triethylamine (1.01 g, 10 mmol) in ethanol (10 ml, 1.0 M
solution) with stir bar. The reaction was heated in 50 °C oil bath for 10
h. Cool the reaction down to room temperature, and add 50 ml ice/water.
The precipitate was filtered and washed with cold ethanol. The title
compound 2.12 g (82 %) as brown power. HRMS ESL-TOF for C14H14N2OS (M+)
found: m/z: 258.0825; Calc. Mass 258.0827. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz): δ
7.38 (d, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.28 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.16 (t, J = 7.8 Hz,
1H), 7.07 (s, 1H), 6.37 (s, 2H), 5.89 (ddt, J =16.8, 10.8, 5.4 Hz, 1H),
5.22 (d, J = 16.8 Hz, 1H), 5.12 (d, J = 10.8 Hz, 1H), 3.97 (t, J = 5.4
Hz, 2H) ppm; 13C NMR (CDCl3, 150 MHz): δ 166.0, 160.8, 134.70 134.1,
128.8, 126.5, 125.0, 124.6, 118.5, 116.1, 109.3, 41.7 ppm.
