$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
N-Allyl-2-amino-5-phenylthiophene-3-carboxamide (C2,6): General Procedure
B (three-component reactions of aldehyde or ketones, cyanoacetamide and
sulfur). In a 20 ml vial added into N-allyl-2-cyanoacetamide (1.24 g, 10
mmol), 2-phenylacetaldehyde (1.20 g, 10 mmol) and sulfur (320 mg, 10
mmol) and triethylamine (1.01 g, 10 mmol) in ethanol (10 ml, 1.0 M
solution) with stir bar. The reaction was heated in 50 °C oil bath for 10
h. Cool the reaction down to room temperature, and add 50 ml ice/water.
The precipitate was filtered and washed with cold ethanol.
2-Amino-N-(2-morpholinoethyl)-5-phenylthiophene-3-carboxamide (C2,4): The
general procedure B was followed employing 2-phenylacetaldehyde (1.20 g,
10 mmol), 2-cyano-N-(2-morpholinoethyl)acetamide (1.97 g, 10 mmol). The
precipitate was filtered to produce the title compound 2.58 g (78 %) as
the dark yellow solid. HRMS ESL-TOF for C17H22N3O2S (M+H+) found: m/z:
332.1455; Calc. Mass 332.1433. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600 MHz): δ 7.43 (d, J =
8.4 Hz, 2H), 7.34 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 2H), 7.22 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 6.99 (s,
1H), 6.43 (s, 1H), 6.23 (s, 2H), 3.75 (t, J = 4.2 Hz, 4H), 3.50 (q, J =
6.0 Hz, 2H), 2.59 (t, J = 6.0 Hz, 2H), 2.51 (brs, 4H) ppm; 13C NMR
(CDCl3, 150 MHz): δ 165.9, 160.3, 134.0, 128.9, 126.7, 125.2, 124.7,
118.2, 109.8, 67.0, 57.2, 53.3, 35.3 ppm.
