$DATUM 2-Amino-5,6-dimethoxy-8H-indeno[2,1-b]thiophene-3-carbonitrile (3,
C14H12N2O2S) To the stirred solution of 24.02 g
2-(2,3-dihydro-5,6-dimethoxy-1H-inden-1-ylidene)malononitrile 2 (0.1 mol)
and 3.2 g elemental sulfur (0.1 mol) in 50 cm3 DMF 5 cm3 triethylamine
was added dropwise over a period of 5 min and the resulting reaction
mixture was stirred for 3 h at room temperature (TLC monitoring,
chloroform-methanol 9:1). The solvent was removed under reduce pressure
and the residue was stirred in 500 cm3 ice-cold water. The separated
solid was filtered, washed with water, dried, and recrystallized from
1,4-dioxane. A faint brown amorphous solid. Yield 20.4 g (75%). M.p.:
231-233°C; Rf = 0.51 (chloroform-methanol 9:1); IR (KBr): ν = 3,400,
3,325, 2,880, 2,210, 1,595, 1,095 cm-1; 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6): δ = 3.61 (s,
2H, CH2), 3.77 (s, 3H, OCH3), 3.78 (s, 3H, OCH3), 7.06 (s, 1H, ArH), 7.20
(s, 1H, ArH), 7.30 (br s, 2H, NH2) ppm; 13C NMR (DMSO-d 6): δ = 32.6,
55.5, 55.6, 101.6, 108.5, 109.7, 116.1, 122.7, 127.7, 130.6, 138.1,
140.4, 146.7, 147.8 ppm; MS (ESI): m/z = 272 (M+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Gewald reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Expedient approach for the synthesis of novel indenothiophene derivatives
